// # Net Submodule Hub -- Zero-Drag
//
// Logline: Unified entry point for the standard net domain library. Re-exports a stable net_mod_* surface for the most-used public API (modules, is_available, http, tcp, tls, udp, dns, url, mime). Phase 3.3 reorg: this domain is now composed of:
//
//   net/protocol/  ← was net/wire/ + net/web_protocols/ + net/http3/ + net/advanced/  (wire + app protocols)
//   net/transport/ ← was net/telecom/ + net/telecom_5g/ + net/telecom_6g/                (telecom/DSP merged)
//   net/mesh/      ← was net/p2p_mesh/ + net/edge/                                       (mesh networking merged)
//   net/telemetry/ ← was net/telecom/ telemetry subset (net/packet capture, ids, dpi)
//   net/sync/      ← was std/sync/                                                       (concurrency primitives)
//   net/actor/     ← was std/actor/                                                      (actor model)
//
// Setup: Imports private net siblings; effectful ops take NetCap / HttpCap / TcpCap / UdpCap at the call site. Pure parser helpers take no caps.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Beat 1: Import the public-API siblings and re-export the modules + is_available surface as net_mod_modules_*, net_mod_is_available.
//   2. Beat 2: Re-export the http surface as net_mod_http_*.
//   3. Beat 3: Re-export the tcp/tls surface as net_mod_tcp_*, net_mod_tls_*.
//   4. Beat 4: Re-export the udp/url/mime surface as net_mod_udp_*, net_mod_url_*, net_mod_mime_*.
//   5. Beat 5: Document the private siblings that external callers must NOT import directly: _law, _theory, _principle, _invariants, _kat, _literature_kat, pay_*, swarm_*, x402_*.

